  "visible_text": "DEEP SPACE NETWORK / HORIZON RELAY\n\nKeep the signal above the curve of Earth.\n\nRead the rotating 3D globe, aim a visible station at each requested spacecraft, keep each transfer moving, and hand off before a horizon loss.\n\nTRACKING GLOBE\ntick 76\nORBITAL VIEW / OUTWARD IS UP\nFULL DISH CONTROL\n\u25c6\nJUNO\n\u25c8\nLUNA\n\u2726\nPIONEER\nCALIFORNIA\nSPAIN\nAUSTRALIA\nROTATING Y AXIS \u00b7 STATION HORIZON IS GEOMETRIC, NOT A MAP EDGE\nFront-facing markers are bright. Dim stations and spacecraft are on the far side; the pale horizon line is the local line-of-sight boundary.\nGROUND STATIONS\nSPAIN\nCALIFORNIA\nJUNO \u00b7 LUNA \u00b7 drag the globe dish\nSPAIN\nPIONEER \u00b7 drag the globe dish\nAUSTRALIA\nnone above horizon \u00b7 drag the globe dish\nSPACECRAFT REQUESTS\n3 / 3\n\u25c6\nJUNO\n20/20\nDELIVERED\n\u25c8\nLUNA\n20/20\nDELIVERED\n\u2726\nPIONEER\n20/20\nDELIVERED\nDIRECT DISH\n\nDrag a bright station dish to a spacecraft marker. Drag again to refresh the pointing as the planet turns.\n\nNO ACTIVE RELAY\n3D CHECK\n\nEach station sits on the sphere's surface. A spacecraft is reachable only when its sightline leaves the station's outward hemisphere; a flat map would give the wrong handoff.\n\nstation\nspacecraft\nabove horizon\nPASS \u00b7 ALL SPACECRAFT RELAYS DELIVERED.\nCERTIFY ALL RELAYS"
